 * 
 * @section dev_class_diag_summary Summary
 * 
 * Device class diagram shows class inheritance hierarchy, dependencies and associations of 
 * each unique SDR device supported by Lime Suite NG library.
 * 
 * ``SDRDevice`` base class is an interface class that declares all possible SDR device control and configuration functions.
 * Since most SDR devices are based on LMS7002M RFIC, a common SDR device class ``LMS7002M_SDRDevice`` is derived from ``SDRDevice``
 * base class. ``LMS7002M_SDRDevice`` defines and overrides configuration and control functions which are common to all SDR devices.
 * Each unique SDR device class is subsequently derived from the ``LMS7002M_SDRDevice`` class and overrides only functions which
 * are specific to each unique SDR device.
 * 
 * Since ``LMS7002M_SDRDevice`` defines common LMS7002M RFIC configuration and control functions it is also dependent on ``LMS7002M``
 *  interface class. ``LMS7002M_SDRDevice`` class also defines the common FPGA control functions and is therefore dependent on the
 * common ``FPGA`` interface class.
 * 
 * Some unique SDR device classes require specific FPGA functionality and are thus derived from the common FPGA interface class.
 * Derived SDR device FPGA classes override only device specific functions and preserve the common FPGA control functionality.
 * Each specific FPGA implementation is associated with specific SDR devices and is used on top of the common FPGA interface, when
 * the SDR device is registered using Lime Suite NG API.
 * 
 * All common and unique SDR device control and configuration functions depend on the virtual serial port interface for communication
 * with the actual SDR device. Virtual serial port interface declares the base communication functions, which are overriden with functions
 * of specific serial port implementation for a each registered and unique SDR device.
 * 
 * @subsection dev_class_legend Diagram legend
 * 
 * Link definitions:
 * 
 * - Solid line with a transparet arrow head body - Inheritance
 * - Dotted line with simple arrow head - Dependency
 * - Solid line with simeple arrow head - Association
 * 
 */